# The answer key to map-order-probe.txt: line N is the file question N was
# written from, in the same order, comments and blank lines skipped on both
# sides. One path per line.
#
# It is written down here rather than kept in a head because the questions were
# always one-per-file by construction (see
# RECORD/2026-09-03.the-map-order-probe.completed.md) and a corpus whose key is
# not on disk can only ever be scored by hand, which is what kept every probe in
# this repository waiting on a person and a model at the same time. With the key
# here, *coverage* — is the target inside what a given order or selector holds —
# is a number this repository can compute in CI, with no model at all. Precision
# still needs one, and that has not changed.
#
# Two targets have moved since the corpus was written, and this file follows the
# tree rather than the other way round: `task.rs` is now `job.rs` (the rename in
# `from-tasks-to-jobs`, which left question 18's wording saying "task type"), and
# the two binary questions were rewritten in the `luu` rename, which is the one
# edit this corpus has ever taken.
#
# Three files this tree has today are asked about by no question — approval.rs,
# sandbox/proxy.rs and tests/stdio.rs, all written after the corpus was. They are
# left out rather than added to: extending an instrument mid-experiment is how a
# number stops being comparable with the one it is being compared to.

crates/agent-core/src/agent.rs
